{
 "_doc": [
  "Declared inputs for rocq/gen/extract/pdl_sites.py, which emits rocq/GenPdl.v.",
  "",
  "NOTHING HERE IS A LINE NUMBER, and that is the point. PdlKernels.v used to",
  "carry the prolog, epilog, write and read positions as integer literals; all",
  "twelve of them were dead within weeks of being written, and a dead literal",
  "checks clean forever because Rocq cannot read a .cu.",
  "",
  "What this file declares is what the CUDA cannot say for itself:",
  "  symbol         -- WHICH __global__ function each Rocq kernel record models.",
  "                    The extractor locates `__global__ void <symbol>(` and",
  "                    refuses unless it occurs exactly once in the declared file.",
  "  produces/      -- WHICH logical buffer a parameter carries, witnessed by the",
  "  consumes          exact source text of the parameter declaration (a text",
  "                    pin, the same device rust/crates/nv-kernels/tests/",
  "                    cuda_ue4m3_subnormal_codec.rs uses against its .cu). The",
  "                    extractor requires the pin to occur exactly once inside",
  "                    that kernel's parameter list, so a rename, a retype or a",
  "                    reorder is a refusal rather than a silently wrong model.",
  "",
  "Everything positional -- prolog, epilog, every store, every dereference -- is",
  "DERIVED from the file on every run and never declared here."
 ],
